{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfbqgq1weQsAtqHpxbvMn", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Use **structlog**. The project settled on it for every module, so production log processing stays uniform. It's already a dependency in `pyproject.toml`, and `src/billing/invoices.py` uses it.\n\n- Put `import structlog` at the top of the module, then `log = structlog.get_logger()`.\n- Don't use the stdlib `logging` module.\n- Event keys are snake_case.\n- Put identifiers in keyword fields, not in the message string. For example, write `log.info(\"invoice_created\", invoice_id=invoice.id)`, not `log.info(f\"created invoice {invoice.id}\")`."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 468, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24211, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 468}, "output_tokens": 199, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f009074b-2af6-489a-a588-48916b10c9e1", "uuid": "deec192c-c33e-442b-bb39-dbff6205e250", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T16:34:06.793Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfbqgpcsb4iAdrh4q2UJ7"}
